# ╔═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
# ║  JOB SEARCH PIPELINE — environment variables                         ║
# ║  Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values. `.env` is gitignored.║
# ║  ⚓ Used by: batch_pipeline.py, daily_pipeline.sh, cron job            ║
# ╚═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LLM API (REQUIRED for scoring + cover letter generation)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-your-real-key-here

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Discord notifications (REQUIRED for daily delivery — ADOPT-8)
#
# We use the SAME Hermes Discord bot that powers ~/Documents/Projects/
# hermes-agent. The bot is already in the channel — no new webhook, no
# new auth surface.
#
# Two ways to wire this:
#
#   (a) Recommended: leave DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN + DISCORD_CHANNEL_ID blank in
#       THIS file. The wrapper sources `~/.hermes/.env` as a fallback and
#       picks up DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN + DISCORD_HOME_CHANNEL automatically.
#       DISCORD_CHANNEL_ID also defaults to DISCORD_HOME_CHANNEL.
#
#   (b) Explicit override: paste the bot token + channel ID here. Useful if
#       you want a dedicated #job-pipeline channel — see DISCORD_CHANNEL_ID.
#
# Override the fallback path by exporting HERMES_ENV=/path/to/other.env
# when Hermes lives somewhere else. See docs/SECRETS.md for the cross-
# project secret-sharing pattern in full.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=«redacted:bot-…»
# DISCORD_CHANNEL_ID=1497988205788663991         # defaults to DISCORD_HOME_CHANNEL

# Optional display name override (both bot and webhook modes respect this)
# DISCORD_USERNAME=Lars Job Pipeline

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Legacy: Discord webhook (ADOPT-7). Still supported for backwards compat —
# the wrapper falls back to webhook mode when bot creds are missing AND this
# is set. Prefer the bot path above; keep this only if you're running the
# dome317 Docker stack against /opt/job-pipeline.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL=https://discord.com/api/webhooks/<your_id>/<your_token>

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Candidate profile (Lars Zimmermann, used by ATS cover-letter templates)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
CANDIDATE_NAME=Lars Zimmermann
CANDIDATE_TITLE=Serial Founder & CTO
CANDIDATE_LOCATION=Brussels, Belgium (open to DACH remote)
CANDIDATE_EMAIL=lars.z@icloud.com
CANDIDATE_PHONE=+32 4xx xx xx xx
CANDIDATE_LINKEDIN=https://www.linkedin.com/in/lars-zimmermann/

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CV Generator
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PHOTO_PATH=./config/photo.png
CANDIDATE_PROFILE=./config/candidate_profile.md

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Proxy for scraping (optional, recommended for Indeed)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PROXY_URL=http://user:pass@proxy-host:12321

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Database paths (defaults to ./data/)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DB_PATH=./data/jobs.db
JOBSPY_DB_PATH=./data/jobspy.db

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pipeline tuning
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set to 1 to use our ATS-safe templates + 4-track WHY-YOU YAML (default).
# Set to 0 to fall back to dome317's stock cover_letter_generator.py.
USE_ATS_TEMPLATES=1

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Google Sheet sync (ADOPT-11) — Sheet → DB approval loop
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Spreadsheet ID from the Sheet URL (between /d/ and /edit). Required for
# `scripts/lars-daily-run.sh --sync-from-sheet`. Without it the sync is a
# no-op (cron-safe: doesn't break the daily run).
GOOGLE_SPREADSHEET_ID=
# Path to the service-account JSON. Defaults to the Hermes-shared SA at
# ~/.hermes/credentials/google-service-account.json when unset. The SA
# needs Editor access on the spreadsheet.
GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=~/.hermes/credentials/google-service-account.json

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Google Sheet delivery (ADOPT-10) — DB → Sheet daily write
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Run `bash scripts/lars-daily-run.sh --sheet` after the daily batch step to
# push the day's scored jobs into a YYYY-MM-DD tab on the same Sheet that
# ADOPT-11 reads from. Reuses GOOGLE_SPREADSHEET_ID + GOOGLE_APPLICATION_
# CREDENTIALS above — no new secrets. Cron mode (no flag) does NOT write
# to the Sheet; you have to opt in by editing the cron line to pass --sheet,
# or by running it manually after the batch.
#
# Setup (one-time, see docs/DAILY-RUN.md §1.3):
#   1. Create a Google Sheet (or pick an existing one) titled "Job Pipeline"
#   2. Share it with the SA's client_email (Editor permission)
#   3. Copy the Sheet ID from the URL (between /d/ and /edit)
#   4. Paste the ID into GOOGLE_SPREADSHEET_ID above
